      "created_at": "2026-04-22T09:30:43Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-04-22T09:30:43Z",
      "body": "Yes, `__msan_unpoison` is available on any platform with (clang-style) MSAN support. That's not all PEP-11 platforms, but that's OK.\n\nWe already use `__msan_unpoison` in a bunch of places.\n\nSee also #11375. 2018 was a different time though :)\nI'd prefer adding a wrapper macro to `pyport.h`, in the spirit of `_Py_MEMORY_SANITIZER` or `_Py_NO_SANITIZE_THREAD`: e.g. `_Py_MSAN_UNPOISON(p, sz)` should call `__msan_unpoison` if it's available, and do nothing otherwise.\n",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
